<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhangye</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhangye is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu-corridor">Hexi Corridor</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu">Gansu</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Known in the past as Ganzhou, it was a garrison and trading town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a>. From the late 9th century it was the seat of the Ganzhou <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghur</a> kingdom, until the Tangut leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-yuanhao">Li Yuanhao</a> captured it in 1028 and it became part of Western Xia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zhangye.jpg" alt="Zhangye" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: YubYub41 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zhangye_Danxia.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
